                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-129",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 157.5, 1010.5, 57.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "D4.calc~",
                    "textcolor": [ 0.666666666666667, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 ]
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-127",
                    "linecount": 13,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 157.0, 8808.44881326845, 487.0, 200.0 ],
                    "text": "-  Shows changes in each of the software releases.\n-  D4 software end user license agreement.\n-  This file. Due to text formatting inconsistencies across Windows and Mac platforms,\n   there are two versions of it, one for each OS.\n-  D4 external help file that is synonymous to the D4.calc~-example.maxpat.\n-  Various files used by demos and example patches.\n-  Text-based introduction that points to D4.introduction.\n-  Example folder used by the D4.mask.renderer to showcase storing, loading, and \n   rendering of the automated mask data.\n-  Rendered data from the renderer-example associated with the test bus. Use with the \n   D4.cell~-example.\n-  Example temperature data of the solar quiescent day, as reflected in the Earth's \n   atmosphere.\n"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-126",
                    "linecount": 2,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 157.0, 8750.44881326845, 487.0, 34.0 ],
                    "text": "-  A collection of demos, including a demo template. See the D4 Use Examples section \n   above for more info on each."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-125",
                    "linecount": 5,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 157.0, 8651.44881326845, 487.0, 75.0 ],
                    "text": "-  A collection of javascript scripts responsible for dynamic creation and processing of low \n   priority elements within the D4 library.\n-  A collection of abstractions that offer different approaches to calculating the \n   per-loudspeaker mask. It is used by the D4.mask.calculator.\n-  A convenience abstraction used by the D4.timeline.editor."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-124",
                    "linecount": 7,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 157.0, 8524.44881326845, 487.0, 103.0 ],
                    "text": "-  Abstraction that passes initializing argument if the argument is non-zero.\n-  A collection of abstractions designed to automate various sine-based spatial source \n   motion. See D4.calc~-example for more info on these.\n-  Abstractions for playing looped and oneshot sounds.\n-  A convenience mixer widget that should be used as a bpatcher. See \n   D4.demo.moogfest2017 for an example of its use.\n-  An example patch that offers D4.ui.mixer~ object presented as a bpatcher."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-123",
                    "linecount": 6,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 157.0, 8411.44881326845, 487.0, 89.0 ],
                    "text": "-  Widget for 3D visualization of the space, its loudspeaker outputs, and the mask.\n-  Abstraction used to dynamically create D4.meter.3D.cell~ abstractions, one per each \n   output channel.\n-  Per-channel abstraction that monitors output and reports it to the D4.3D.visualizer~.\n-  Per-channel abstraction to be used as a bpatcher as part of the 2D monitors.\n-  A collection of 2D output monitors for various loudspeaker configurations."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-122",
                    "linecount": 10,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 157.0, 8243.44881326845, 487.0, 144.0 ],
                    "text": "-  Used to calculate mask based on the incoming image data. Comes in two versions: \n   multithreaded (default) and singlethreaded one with a .single suffix.\n-  Widget for visual editing of the mask that has D4.mask.calculator embedded. Alternative\n   version is provided that is designed to work with the D4.calc~-example-custom.\n-  Widget/abstraction designed to store, load, and render mask data into continuous \n   automation.\n-  Widget/abstraction for playing back both the mask and other (positional or pos) \n   automation.\n-  A DAW-like widget for loading, automation, and exproting of azimuth, elevation, ramp \n   up/down, gain, and radius."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-121",
                    "linecount": 17,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 157.0, 7978.448813268449, 487.0, 241.0 ],
                    "text": "-  Responsible for dynamically generating output for each channel of the D4.calc~ and \n   whose output is forwarded to the D4.dac~ or the main output.\n-  poly~ optimized variant of the D4~ that toggles output of each channel based on \n   whether it has anyhting to output.\n-  Core object that uses the D4 library, and D4~ to process and output one multichannel\n    stream, including mask, radius, and ramp data.\n-  poly~  optimized variant of the D4.calc~.\n-  Various examples of the D4.calc~ variants.\n-  Individual cell calculator for each of teh D4.calc~ output channels. Offers a number of \n   variants, including the poly~ optimized one. By default, D4.calc~ utilizes D4.cell~ unless \n   user overrides it with the second creation argument.\n-  Individual cell for the D4.dac~.\n-  D4's maing output that dynamically generates output channels and supplants the \n   regular dac~ output to circumvent the use of patch cords.\n-  Main widget for controlling the main out levels. By default it should be used as a GUI.\n   Can be also used as a non-GUI abstraction.\n-  Calibration files for various multichannel loudspeaker configurations."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-120",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 157.0, 7906.448813268449, 487.0, 48.0 ],
                    "text": "-  Core external that needs to be authorized and is responsible for key calculations.\n-  Java-based class to be used with mxj object used for storing, loading, and rendering of\n    the mask data."
                }
            },
